        <body>
            <div xml:id="d120">

                <pb facs="0175" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/636–637.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-05-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 21, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1162.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copy
                    in translation of a note received to-day from the Wai-wu Pu conveying its hearty
                    thanks to the American Government for its assistance in this matter.</p>
                <p>I presume that a similar note has been sent to each of the other powers
                    represented on the commission.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d120-a1.xml" xpointer="d120-a1"/>
            </div>
